{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1234337-2e-do-raksha-have-a-dice-limit-plus-other-raksha-related-questions","id":1234337,"title":"[2e] Do raksha have a dice limit? Plus other raksha related questions!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-12T11:27:41-07:00","id":1234337,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> [2e] Do raksha have a dice limit? Plus other raksha related questions!","content":"Do the raksha have a set maximum dice-cap for dice added by charms? I\u2019m struggling to find a hard-and-fast rule on it in Graceful Wicked Masques, which is hardly surprising. Each individual charm generally includes a limit, but I can\u2019t see an overall \u201cno combination of charms can add more than x\u201d, apart from with respect to shaping dice pools.<br /> <br /> If there isn't one, do people think that's an intentional omission, to make the raksha even more different to play than traditional Exalts, or is it just another GWM-ism? And if it's the latter, what would you suggest as an appropriate dice-cap for raksha? Essence? Essence + Ability? Essence + Related Grace?<br /> <br /> As a corollary, do dice from oneiromancies and adjurations that simulate raksha charms count against that limit? For instance, if I use Elegant Muse Attitude as a charm to add dice, would you say an oneiromancy making use of the same charm would stack? If so, does it stack beyond the normal Essence dice limit for that charm (as it\u2019s technically a bonus from an item)? What if it was a bonus from a different one of the set of merged charms?<br /> <br /> Okay, I\u2019m clearly way too deep into GWM-brain, but still, any advice would be great.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11800-kajata","name":"Kajata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-12T13:12:59-07:00","id":1234377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kajata</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1234337-2e-do-raksha-have-a-dice-limit-plus-other-raksha-related-questions#post1234337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If there isn't one, do people think that's an intentional omission, to make the raksha even more different to play than traditional Exalts, or is it just another GWM-ism?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say it's an artefact of how the book was made. As I understand it, First Edition Raksha had basically now die-adders, with the logic that they instead relied on their native capacity to have high Attributes and Abilities. I think Second Edition kind of wanted to sustain that, except it didn't really work with the overall system, so something needed to be slotted in a bit artlessly.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T08:41:02-07:00","id":1234654,"title":"","content":"Have you checked the errata for GWM? I vaguely recall a cap being introduced there, although a cursory ctrl+f didn't reveal it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Raksha are my fae-vorite.<br /> <br /> Reincarnation of magnificentmomo.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1542-morosemorgan","name":"MoroseMorgan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T08:52:17-07:00","id":1234656,"title":"","content":"I know I'm not helping, but I'm wondering: when would this come up? I don't recall Raksha having dice-adders that don't have built-in limits on the number of dice added, so how would you ever add more than 3ish dice?<br /> <br /> And if you did, you did it with custom Charms, right? So you might as well write up your own limit. In which case I would argue for either Essence + relevant Grace because it's flavorful, but if you find it too fidgety to have to adjudicate which Grace applies, maybe Attribute + Essence, or just Attribute? I feel like Raksha are more defined by what they are, even if that's metaphysically a lie, than by what they learn, or do, so I wouldn't go for ability as a limiter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat","name":"Cheshire Cat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"502"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T12:15:10-07:00","id":1234736,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure it's supposed to be (essence) in the errata because that's the limit of their native dice adders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-13T14:06:34-07:00","id":1234769,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/903-cheshire-cat\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar903_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"903\" data-vbnamecard=\"903\">Cheshire Cat</a> I was mostly thinking of situations where combinations of dice-adders, assumptions, and other bonuses might push it higher. Hell even using multiple dice adders would seem to work, if there's no specific dice cap.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat said, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar7_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"7\" data-vbnamecard=\"7\">Lioness</a> is right, the errata does institute a clear dice-cap of Essence! Thanks for the help all!<br /> <br /> Okay, one further question; I've heard people talk about Raksha affecting the flow of time in the Wyld. I appreciate that shaping actions can be quite flexible in terms of how long they last (basically, only lasting as long as they need to in order to come to pass or not), but is there anything explicit about raksha being able to use shaping to change the rate at which time flows in the wyld?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11800-kajata","name":"Kajata","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11800_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}